        "Massive PE: hemodynamic instability (SBP <90 or ↓40 from baseline). Submassive: normal BP + RV strain (↑troponin, ↑BNP, RV dilation on echo/CT). Non-massive: stable. ECG: sinus tachycardia (most common), S1Q3T3, new RBBB",
        "Massive PE: systemic thrombolysis (alteplase 100mg over 2h) or surgical embolectomy. Submassive: anticoagulation ± catheter-directed thrombolysis (PERT team). Non-massive: anticoagulation (LMWH bridge → warfarin, or DOAC preferred — rivaroxaban or apixaban)",
        "S1Q3T3 in PE: deep S wave in lead I + Q wave + inverted T wave in lead III. PERC rule (if low pretest probability AND all 8 criteria met → no further workup needed). D-dimer: high sensitivity (~95%) — negative D-dimer excludes PE in low-to-moderate pretest probability."
