        "Calf DVT (below popliteal): low PE risk — anticoagulate or serial US monitoring. Proximal DVT (above popliteal — popliteal, femoral, iliac): high PE risk → anticoagulate. Phlegmasia cerulea dolens: massive ileofemoral DVT → limb-threatening ischemia",
